/* 
  Anatomy of a JWT 
  It consists of 3 parts separated by dots: Header.Payload.Signature
  Example: eyJhbGci.eyJ1c2VySW.SflKxwRJSMeKKF2
*/

// 1. The Header (Algorithm used)
{ "alg": "HS256", "typ": "JWT" }

// 2. The Payload (The actual data. Do not put passwords here!)
{
  "userId": 123,
  "role": "admin",
  "exp": 1716500000 // Expiration timestamp
}

// 3. The Signature
// The server takes the Header + Payload, and hashes them together 
// using a highly secret password (SECRET_KEY) that only the server knows.
// If a hacker alters the Payload to "role": "admin", the Signature will 
// mathematically fail verification on the server!
